---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
---

<Docs slug="verify">
      <h2 id="vf-run">Run it</h2>
      <pre class="code"><code>cue verify --base-url http://localhost:3000</code></pre>
      <h2 id="vf-verdicts">Verdicts</h2>
      <div class="table"><table>
        <thead><tr><th>Verdict</th><th>Means</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><code>PASS</code></td><td>Every route was checked and matches.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>PARTIAL</code></td><td>Some routes were checked; the rest were not.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>NOT VERIFIED</code></td><td>Nothing was looked at, for example no <code>--base-url</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>FAIL</code></td><td>Drift, an unreachable route or an unreadable file.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>EMPTY</code></td><td>Nothing has been surveyed yet.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <h2 id="vf-ci">In CI</h2>
      <p><code>--ci</code> exits 1 on <code>FAIL</code> only. <code>--ci=strict</code> exits 1 unless the verdict is <code>PASS</code>, so "nobody looked" is never a green build.</p>
      <pre class="code"><code>cue verify --base-url $STAGING_URL --ci=strict</code></pre>
      <h2 id="vf-refresh">Re-survey one route</h2>
      <p>When a single route is stale, survey that route again instead of crawling the whole app.</p>
    
</Docs>
